# DEPRECATED — do not apply

This rule is **superseded by Constitution §21 (Dead Code Removal)** at
`.specify/memory/constitution.md` and by `.cursor/rules/compact-code.mdc`.

The previous policy (never delete dead code, scratchpads, or commented logic)
is **reversed**:

- Dead functions, unused imports, commented-out logic, and stale experimental
  files whose last caller is gone MUST be removed in the same change.
- "Will deleting this break anything?" — if no, delete it. Git history is the
  reference archive.

**This file is empty by intent.** Do not extend it. If you arrived here from a
stale cross-reference, update the reference to point to Constitution §21 instead
(see `.cursor/rules/documentation-sync.mdc`).
